{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_2grgvmdetg4bgrqzzff7o6yabhpaieirllfgmwrdmzjq6dalzy4q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The test passes. The implementation is complete:\n\n## Summary\n\nI translated the C `cfsm` (Finite State Machine) library to safe, idiomatic Rust by implementing all 5 `unimplemented!()` bodies in `src/cfsm.rs`:\n\n1. **`new()`** — Returns a `CfsmCtx` with all fields set to `None`.\n2. **`cfsm_init()`** — Mirrors the C `cfsm_init` which assigns `(instanceData, 0, 0, 0)`: stores the instance data and clears all handlers.\n3. **`cfsm_transition()`** — Calls the existing `on_leave` handler (if present), clears all handlers, then calls the new `enter_func` (if provided). Each handler call wraps `&mut *self` in `Some(Box::new(...))` to match the expected callback signature.\n4. **`cfsm_process()`** — Delegates to `on_process` if defined.\n5. **`cfsm_event()`** — Delegates to `on_event` with the given `event_id` if defined.\n\nNo `unsafe` was needed in `cfsm.rs`, no FFI/`libc`, and no dependencies were added. The single test (`test_main`) passes, and only the unmodifiable `src/bin/test.rs` produces warnings."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":713,"cache_read_input_tokens":39137,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":713,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"40d1c9f9-bd29-4892-8441-ed1e5cdb2d9e","uuid":"4625d9a0-5c16-480d-9164-b1b9358f0190"}
